{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands","id":1526017,"title":"Spectres in the Shadowlands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-27T13:55:01-08:00","id":1526017,"title":"Spectres in the Shadowlands","content":"Those spectres who have Fetters can manifest in the Shadowlands. This includes Dopplegangers and Mortwights as well as some Nephwracks (the books are inconsistent about this, but even if their corpus displays the effects of Oblivion, I don't see why they might not still have Fetters). However, they are not able to see the Skinlands normally, they can do that only if they have the right amount of Shroud Rending. Therefore, spectres in the Shadowlands see a lot of it as empty. They don't see all things that wraiths do. They only see those parts that are truly part of the Shadowlands (Dark Reflections states the Shadowlands are empty except for other wraiths and spectres. I would assume it should also include anything that originates from that side of the Shroud - other plasmic creatures, Stygian steel, artifacts, nihils, etc.). This might not be an issue for Mortwights and Nephwracks, but I think this should cause an issue for Dopplegangers pretending they are normal wraiths.<br /> <br /> Should Spectres be impacted by the Rule of Ouch if they don't see things in the Skinlands? Presumably not. They don't care if a truck runs over them like a wraith would. It doesn't exist for them. But presumably if they use Shroud Rending, then what they can sense becomes &quot;real enough&quot; and the Rule of Ouch applies.<br /> <br /> But this should cause a real problem for Dopplegangers infiltrating wraith society. Unless they have Shroud Rending, they just cannot act like a normal wratih does. They can't see or dwell in the reflections of Skinland buildings like many wraiths do. They cannot talk about that TV episode the other wraiths are watching and talking about. They can't act like they should if people or vehicles or other Skinland activity should be impacting them. It would be very obvious they must be a spectre.<br /> <br /> That would mean the only Dopplegangers who could truly infiltrate wraithly society would be ones with a good rank in Shroud Rending. But I don't think that was the intention. Dopplegangers shouldn't need to wait a long time until they develop a high level of Shroud Rending. Newly created Dopplegangers should be able to infiltrate best when their corpus is least scarred by Oblivion, and their old friends haven't noticed they've been gone for a long time. Waiting until they have sufficient ranks in Shroud Rending not to be caught works against that. And the description of Dopplegangers never hint that this is the case.<br /> <br /> So do you think this is just a goof by the rules? Is this how you run it anyway? Or should there be a rule that says Dopplegangers (though not Mortwights) can see the Skinlands normally as long as they still have Fetters? Perhaps this could be modified that each dot of Fetters effectively gives them an equivalent rank in Shroud-Rending, so that not all Dopplegangers are equally adept. That would enable Dopplegangers to actually infiltrate wraith society off the bat, assuming they have sufficient Fetters. And it would give them time enough to learn Shroud Rending if they wanted, and not at the expense of other Dark Arcanoi they might have wanted to learn first.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Has this been addressed already, but I simply don't know about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T07:38:39-08:00","id":1526066,"title":"","content":"I would look at it as an unintentional bug. Much of wraith society takes place outside of areas where the rule of ouch regularly matters, so a Doppleganger could probably get quite far even if they couldn't see the living. However, it would be too easy to block Doppleganger infiltration if a Necropolis could just institute a monthly Crowded Mall Obstacle Course. <br /> <br /> Letting Spectres with Fetters see the living would indeed solve the problem. Barring that, I'd shoot for a middle ground. My initial thought would be something like this:<br /> <br /> The rule of ouch always applies. Deathsight gives enough information that an attentive Spectre can move out of the way of anything larger than a housecat. They won't necessarily know what they are dodging without a roll, though, so the rule of Excuse Me doesn't work for them. Any attempt to see any detail in the Skinlands requires an actual roll, and the lack of Lifesight increases the difficulty.<br /> <br /> It also might work to give Spectres the ability to see the Skinlands for a scene at the cost of automatically gaining a point of Composure.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T12:42:42-08:00","id":1526077,"title":"","content":"I agree it is an unintentional bug. The writers just did not think things through sufficiently.<br /> <br /> I now wonder if I should simply take the sentence &quot;Unless a spectre knows Shroud-Rending, the Shadowlands will always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; to mean that spectres do not have Lifesense and cannot sense the living. But non-living objects from the Skinlands still appear as they would through Deathsight. I was taking &quot;always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; very literally. Perhaps I am not supposed to. That would eliminate 90%+ of the problems I have, especially for the Rule of Ouch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T13:45:10-08:00","id":1526079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526077#post1526077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now wonder if I should simply take the sentence &quot;Unless a spectre knows Shroud-Rending, the Shadowlands will always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; to mean that spectres do not have Lifesense and cannot sense the living. But non-living objects from the Skinlands still appear as they would through Deathsight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would make sense, cause Spectres can see anything in the Skinlands that's Oblivion-tainted and we know all physical structures look decayed when perceived from the Shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T09:38:22-08:00","id":1526115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526077#post1526077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree it is an unintentional bug. The writers just did not think things through sufficiently.<br /> <br /> I now wonder if I should simply take the sentence &quot;Unless a spectre knows Shroud-Rending, the Shadowlands will always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; to mean that spectres do not have Lifesense and cannot sense the living. But non-living objects from the Skinlands still appear as they would through Deathsight. I was taking &quot;always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; very literally. Perhaps I am not supposed to. That would eliminate 90%+ of the problems I have, especially for the Rule of Ouch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, given that Spectres do have Deathsight, they should have no problems seeing the non-living objects of the Skinlands the way Wraiths do. Perhaps even more worn down, though that would just be for dramatic effect.<br /> <br /> I would go one step further. Deathsight does apply to the living as well, especially when they are sick, injured, or will soon be hurt. That should show up to Spectres as freefloating wounds or miasma. It wouldn't be enough for a Spectre to actually see the living with any detail (except for the actively dying), but it would be enough to avoid colliding with most living things (except something young like a baby elephant).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T11:39:15-08:00","id":1526126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526115#post1526115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps even more worn down, though that would just be for dramatic effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Reflections mentions that their Deathsight does show a more decayed version of the world than what wraiths see with their Deathsight because Oblivion is stronger in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526115#post1526115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go one step further. Deathsight does apply to the living as well, especially when they are sick, injured, or will soon be hurt. That should show up to Spectres as freefloating wounds or miasma. It wouldn't be enough for a Spectre to actually see the living with any detail (except for the actively dying), but it would be enough to avoid colliding with most living things (except something young like a baby elephant).</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Reflections states that spectres have a Deathsense. Deathsense allows spectres to sense Oblivion in others. Spetres can tell how strong a Shadow a Wraith has because it means Oblivion is stronger in them. It also allows them to sense Oblivion's &quot;black light&quot; across the Shroud - humans close to death or who have <i>strong</i> Dark Passions, and vampires burn bright with Oblivion so they are always detected by Deathsense as well. <br /> <br /> So these are exceptions to the normal rule that spectres don't see anything in the Skinlands. But what they see is some version of the black radiance of Oblivion, not really what that thing is in itself. <br /> <br /> I would also think that Risen would be detected the same way as vampires, as well as any other thing that would be considered to be undead (zombies created by Necromancy, Corpse Minions or Demon Bound created by Thaumaturgy, Meat Puppets mentioned in 1e Book of the Wyrm). There's an obvious source of Oblivion on the other side of the Shroud.<br /> <br /> So what you say is more or less covered in material, but it's classified as something different from Deathsight and Lifesight. However, in order to determine what exactly is burning bright with Oblivion, I think the spectre would need to use Shroud Rending. Otherwise they only know something strongly is burning strongly with Oblivion on the other side.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T08:21:01-08:00","id":1526185,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's exactly what I was going for, though I did not distinguish between Deathsight and Deathsense. I think I missed the change in terminology in Dark Reflections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T18:31:01-08:00","id":1526336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526077#post1526077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree it is an unintentional bug. The writers just did not think things through sufficiently.<br /> <br /> I now wonder if I should simply take the sentence &quot;Unless a spectre knows Shroud-Rending, the Shadowlands will always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; to mean that spectres do not have Lifesense and cannot sense the living. But non-living objects from the Skinlands still appear as they would through Deathsight. I was taking &quot;always be empty to her save for wraiths and other spectres&quot; very literally. Perhaps I am not supposed to. That would eliminate 90%+ of the problems I have, especially for the Rule of Ouch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is... How I have always thought about it. I never thought that the Shadowlands were simply a black desert without buildings or mountains or nothing. I just always assumed that the Spectres couldn't see the living, but they still could see a ruined city and a rusty truck coming their way.<br /> <br /> I don't know why you thought otherwise, or why I never thought of it as you do, but that idea just simply never even crossed my mind before","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T21:20:38-08:00","id":1526343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526336#post1526336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why you thought otherwise, or why I never thought of it as you do, but that idea just simply never even crossed my mind before</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just because the sentence said &quot;always be empty&quot;. That's quite an absolute. Empty means a void. If it said &quot;cannot see the living&quot; or similar, I'd assume everything else that was a reflection of the Skinlands could be seen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T08:36:00-08:00","id":1526361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526343#post1526343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was just because the sentence said &quot;always be empty&quot;. That's quite an absolute. Empty means a void. If it said &quot;cannot see the living&quot; or similar, I'd assume everything else that was a reflection of the Skinlands could be seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I believe that was a miscommunication from the part of the writers. Still it's weird that my brain didn't make the same association. Maybe my right hemisphere just thought that it would be nonsensical and immediately discarded it. But I doubt that was truly the writers intent - as you explained, it would make Spectres infiltration basically impossible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T19:52:14-08:00","id":1526491,"title":"","content":"I always assumed it meant empty <i>of people</i>, but spectres would still be aware of (more ruined versions of) buildings and objects that regular wraiths perceive in the Shadowlands. Everything might look post-apocalyptic, but it would occupy the same space as the regular counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T11:25:27-08:00","id":1526522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1526017-spectres-in-the-shadowlands?p=1526491#post1526491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed it meant empty <i>of people</i>, but spectres would still be aware of (more ruined versions of) buildings and objects that regular wraiths perceive in the Shadowlands. Everything might look post-apocalyptic, but it would occupy the same space as the regular counterparts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes more sense, and I think that is how I was supposed to interpret that sentence. You (and many others) were just smarter than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T14:43:00-08:00","id":1526527,"title":"","content":"It took me more time than I care to admit to realize that the Underworld was really dark, despite terms like &quot;The Sunless Sea.&quot; Also, to this day I rarely find two people who envision the Tempest the same way.<br /> <br /> Wraith is a deliberately alien setting and its not surprising that we occasionally miss something or envision things differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 12-11-2023, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}